cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "x² + 1 — research repo"
abstract: >-
  Instrumentation and notes for an attack on Landau's fourth problem (infinitely
  many primes of the form x²+1) via the Friedlander–Iwaniec asymptotic sieve
  reformulated over the Gaussian integers. The repository records a located
  structural obstruction — the Type I/II sieve framework cannot capture x²+1,
  because the relevant off-diagonal counting function is a 0/1 indicator — and a
  body of Diophantine results on the underlying incidence, which is a bipartite
  Diophantine tuple with property BD₂(−1). Every claim carries an enforced
  epistemic status checked by the test suite.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/heidrickla/x2plus1-research"
url: "https://github.com/heidrickla/x2plus1-research"
authors:
